  "question": "Does the reported 2003 donation of a Wenhui historical newspaper CD-ROM to the National Library of China create a distinct lawful route toward the 1951-08-18 target page, and can the donated object be bound to a current NLC item identity?",
  "answer": "Yes at the historical digital-object/provenance level, but not yet at item/page level. A directly retrieved 2003 contemporary web reprint labeled as sourced from 文汇报 reports donation to NLC of 《文汇报60年报纸光盘》, 13 discs, with declared coverage from 1938-01 through 1998-12 containing all text and images and supporting date/name lookup. That declared range includes 1951-08-18. However no CD-ROM target query is performed and target article presence is not proved. Current first-party NLC entry/service pages expose catalog/digital-resource/optical-disc service context but do not name the CD-ROM or expose an item-level record. The 2005 IFLA archive PDF is not directly retrievable on the controlling runner, so any '61-year' object remains separate and uncollapsed.",
